---
/**
 * The Contact island's script, and nothing else.
 *
 * It lives in its own component so `ContactPage.astro` can decide whether to
 * render it: a `<script>` written inside a conditional expression is not
 * processed by Astro, but a component rendered conditionally is. When the
 * enquiry form is off (`availability.ts`), this component is not rendered and
 * the page emits no `<script>` for the island.
 *
 * Note that Astro still BUILDS the chunk for any component in a page's import
 * graph (`core/build/plugins/plugin-analyzer.js` adds every `.astro` module's
 * scripts to `discoveredScripts`), so an unreferenced `_astro/ContactIsland*.js`
 * may still exist in `dist/`. That is why the island itself carries no
 * development-only user-facing text (see `statusText` in `islands/contact.ts`).
 */
---

<script>
  import '../../scripts/islands/contact';
</script>
